      "content": "I'll read the original test and CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that when the edit distance between a 1-character `CharBuffer` and a 10-character string far exceeds threshold=1, the result is -1. Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`charBuffer0`, `integer0`, `levenshteinDetailedDistance0`) with descriptive ones, removes unused imports, and adds a concise Javadoc comment explaining the scenario: a 1-character input vs. a 10-character string with threshold=1 yields distance=-1 because the actual edit distance far exceeds the threshold."
